  "id": "DrugBank_DB00724 - MONDO_5647",
  "verbalization": "Imiquimod, a topical immunomodulator, is implicated in the treatment of common warts through its ability to induce an inflammatory response. This mechanism is supported by its indication for common warts and its association with trichloroacetate and cianidanol, both of which are also indicated for the same condition. The evidence suggests that Imiquimod may exert a role in the pathogenesis of anogenital human papillomavirus (HPV) infection through an inflammatory pathway, as these compounds are linked to the same clinical indication. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Imiquimod to anogenital HPV infection highlights a potential mechanism involving immune modulation, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering immunomodulatory effects in the context of viral infections, particularly in the anogenital tract.",
